# Model weights, wherever they land.
#
# The rules below scope weights to models/ and vendor/. That was not enough:
# a download whose `cd` silently failed wrote midi_rwkv.pth to the repo root and
# it was committed. These patterns are path-independent on purpose -- a weight
# is never a source file, regardless of which directory a script was standing in.
*.pth
*.pt
*.ckpt
*.safetensors
*.bin
*.gguf
*.onnx

# Exception: Basic Pitch's shard is a browser asset, not a server-side model
# weight. It is small, it is served from public/, and the whole point of it is
# that transcription runs on the device. It predates these rules and stays.
!public/models/**

# --- AI Musician service ---
# Model weights are never committed. See third_party/MANIFEST.md rule 5 and
# models/manifest.json; fetch with scripts/models/bootstrap.{sh,ps1}.
models/*
!models/.gitkeep
!models/manifest.json
!models/README.md

# Upstream source is fetched at pinned SHAs by scripts/vendor/bootstrap.{sh,ps1}
vendor/*
!vendor/.gitkeep
!vendor/README.md

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.venv/
.ruff_cache/
services/**/*.egg-info/
